=== Query Timeout Demo (client-side read_timeout) ===

[setup] Created cookbook_timeout_demo and committed initial row
[1] Writer holds an uncommitted lock on id=1
[2] Second connection (read_timeout=2s) attempts the same UPDATE...
[3] Timed out as expected: OperationalError: socket communication failed
    -> a client-side read_timeout bounds an operation blocked on a lock
[4] Writer released the lock and dropped the table; timed-out socket discarded

--- Key points ---
  pycubrid.connect(..., read_timeout=SECONDS) bounds blocked/slow operations
  Prefer a client-side read_timeout over relying on server lock_timeout
  A timed-out connection's socket is dead -- discard it, never reuse it
